invariant: INV-43
file: p256_wide_verify_point.c
catches: p256_verify_equiv_test
reason: the host verifier's general Jacobian addition gives the point at
  infinity for two equal points, where the sum is their double. The
  addition formula has no answer for that case, so the file tests for it
  and doubles. A random signature meets it one time in 2^256; the case of
  bin/p256_verify_equiv_test under the key G with u1 equal to u2 adds a
  multiple of the key to the same multiple of G at the top digit, and
  wants the signature taken.

